    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** and **Dylan Beavers** headline the LawDog lineup, both leveraging an elite matchup against Littell to earn the highest daily efficiency scores of 71.46 and 68.38, respectively. The heavy weighting toward these two is driven by an excellent park environment and favorable opposing SP_xERA of 4.82, though both carry a 30% rain risk warning that requires monitoring. **Jonathan Aranda** remains a high-floor start at 70.47, benefiting significantly from his position in the two-hole and an advantageous matchup against Me. Kelly (4.85 xERA). Meanwhile, **Daulton Varsho** (68.45) is a priority play not just for his park-adjusted projection, but because Rocker\u2019s slow delivery profile creates a prime opportunity to chase the stolen bases we desperately need to stay competitive in the standings.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Luis Arraez**, who posted a 40.19 efficiency score. While he remains a steady contact option, he was pushed out by higher-upside plays against weaker pitching, specifically the matchup-proof numbers of **Lawrence Butler** (60.04) and the strategic slotting of **Tyler Freeman** (62.36). We are navigating a difficult matchup for **Matt Chapman** against Sale (3.01 xERA), but his leadoff spot and wind-aided park boost allow him to squeeze into the lineup over **Jung Hoo Lee**, whose 34.52 score failed to meet our internal 40.0 floor. **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Gavin Sheets** represent our most marginal starters today; while they provide necessary defensive and power depth, their projections are suppressed by strong opposing arms in Rasmussen and Sheehan, respectively. Keep a close watch on the weather for our OF1 and OF5, as the rain threat in that specific matchup represents the primary volatility in today's scoring outlook.",
